  "rules": [
    "Legacy-v1 /turn atomically records finalized caller text then calls Jev. Bob-task-v1 uses /caller-turns and /task; Jev does not run in its live action path. Worker/model cannot submit workflow authority, tenant IDs, timestamps or confirmation booleans.",
    "caller-turns records authenticated finalized text only and grants no write. Bob-task-v1 (voice agent v2, VA-C1) has no readback or confirmation: task commands are start, record, finish and cancel; any finalized caller turn of the call is accepted and no workflow revision is required. record validates each field on its own, returns accepted and rejected, replays a repeated operationId, and saves a service request with a receipt in the same call that completes it. requests/readback is legacy-only. Legacy confirmation retains its classified-turn binding.",
    "Every terminal path (task-end, ending, terminal, caller end, deadline, provider failure, share or erasure end) turns each unfinished task with a goal or any field into exactly one Needs review record in outcomes (service_request, appointment_lookup) or cases (complaint), with fields, missingFields, endedBecause and reviewStatus needs_review. The task's noteRecordId makes this idempotent. Record reads add nextStep, computed by server/api/next-step.js.",
    "Server loads current callerTurnId AND sequence, workflow/field/readback revisions and hash within its transaction. Confirmation turn must follow the readback. Fields corrected after readback invalidate confirmation.",
    "Workflow events are server-persisted audit records, never an arbitrary worker mutation endpoint. /turn and typed action routes create events.",
    "Owner history extends existing /v1/agents/:id and /v1/workspaces/:id families. Authenticated membership and claimed resource ownership are mandatory. Never scope by public URL or shared agent alone.",
    "Escalation preempts intake. Atomically enter ending before a single idempotent case attempt capped at two seconds. Closing audio <=3 seconds or remaining deadline. Termination works on storage or TTS failure; no reconnect.",
    "When ending or terminal, reject new request mutations. Only reconcile previously committed receipts or the bounded escalation operation bound to that ending transition. Ending/terminal endpoints are idempotent and revision checked.",
    "No private request/case enters retrieval. Retrieval supported results contain eligible facts and supporting passages from pinned knowledge. Unknown/conflicting/stale facts cannot support answers.",
    "Operation ID and payload hash bind append-only receipts. Exact retry returns original receipt; changed payload conflicts. Lookup unavailable never means not_found.",
    "Published schemas are integration interfaces, not evidence the planned routes or transaction checks are implemented.",
    "GET demo status preserves mode and all existing server timer fields. GET demo result additionally returns append-only requests/cases/lookups/receipts for that scoped demo before claim. appointmentRequest is a nullable legacy unconfirmed draft, never a saved outcome; new UI consumes the outcome arrays. Both responses retain requestId/version in the existing flat HTTP envelope.",
    "CAS continuity: caller-turn recording does not change workflow revision and returns its current workflowRevision. /turn increments revision once for its committed decision and returns workflow.revision. Each successful fields/readback/confirmation/lookup/request/case action increments revision once and returns the committed workflowRevision; failed or replayed operations return the current state via the conflict or original receipt and never silently advance it.",
    "Ending atomically advances both session stateRevision and workflow revision; ending response returns both. Its bounded escalation uses that returned expectedWorkflowRevision. Terminal response returns both resulting revisions. Idempotent replay returns the original response unchanged. A stale-revision error includes currentWorkflowRevision/currentStateRevision for explicit reload/reconciliation; it never authorizes blind retry of a changed payload.",
    "Confirmation response workflowRevision is the committed workflow revision to pass to saveRequestInput.expectedWorkflowRevision. Field/readback revisions track confirmed payload separately and must not be substituted for workflow CAS revision.",
    "Routes marked planned_post_onboarding are the owner, guest, builder and worker routes of the post-onboarding slice, described by post-onboarding.schema.json. They are implemented behind FRONTLINE_POST_ONBOARDING. Responses are flat like every other route; validate the payload after stripping requestId and version. Owner routes use the fl_auth session and claimed-target ownership, guest routes only the fl_guest capability, builder routes a builder session or a read-only flb_ credential, and the worker route the existing internal worker authentication. GET and DELETE routes with a query describe it in the request ref."
  ],
